// GenericSecretsService — encrypted namespace:key KV store with versioning,
// soft-delete, and batch operations.
//
// Extends the vault plugin to serve general-purpose secrets (API keys,
// channel credentials, JWT secrets, auth tokens) alongside the existing
// PasswordVaultService. Shares the same AES-256-GCM encryption, kernel-
// backed storage, and master key — only the data model differs: generic
// secrets are simple namespace:key→value pairs (no VaultEntry schema,
// no TOTP).
//
// Consumer: sudowork SecretStoreClient (replaces HTTP /api/v2/secrets).
// Namespace conventions:
//   channel:{type}:{pluginId}  → token, appSecret, clientSecret, ...
//   provider:{providerId}      → api_key, access_key_id, secret_access_key
//   auth:acp:{backend}         → auth_token
//   auth:jwt                   → webui_secret, webui_secret:{userId}
//
// Protocol version: 2026.1

